{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", collected by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"code":"0x6576_6E74","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSetsRuntime for the expansion, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads the set for its users:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@_exported import LinkerSetsRuntime","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSetsRuntime.LinkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSetsRuntime module. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library that imports it without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “cannot find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘LinkerSetsRuntime’ in scope” unless each one imports it too. The library depends on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSetsRuntime, not LinkerSets: its own plugin writes the records, so it needn’t build"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets’ plugin as well. The re-export also puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvents.all"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set is read in one place."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading","level":3},{"code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type, is refused with a message, as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"reference"},{"text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Routes","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Migrations","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)"},{"text":", read as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>"},{"text":", sorted by a version the migration declares.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dependency registrations","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"type":"topic","title":"Finding records","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","title":"Platforms and linking","abstract":[{"text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","abstract":[{"text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it.","type":"text"}],"title":"Declaring a kind","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","title":"What the macros refuse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"type":"topic","title":"LinkerSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"type":"topic","title":"LinkerSetKind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"}}}